# Efficient layout fixes

For a small visual fix, measure the window the user is looking at, edit once, measure that same window again, then stop.

- Change only the reported problem. A clear gap and a shared edge are enough. Do not invent a new size curve.
- Do not resize through other widths unless the user asked, or a number shows a screen they already accepted has broken.
- Fold a few pixels of mismatch into the same edit. Do not open a second investigation.
- Trust the measured pixels. Do not screenshot to re-judge a number already measured.
